{
  "$comment": "Trace Commons glass design tokens: the one source for the native macOS app (and, later, any other shell). Light and dark: every colour has a dark value and, where it differs, a light one, and follows the person's system appearance (D2 revised), purple brand (D3), SF Pro and SF Mono (R2): every type step is a macOS text style, so it follows the system text size, and its size is that style's size at the default setting (number was 28 in #1146; largeTitle is 26). Seeded from #1146's tauri-desktop/frontend/src/design-system/tokens at 09a26c0d. Edit here, then run scripts/design-tokens/generate.py; a Swift test fails if the generated file drifts.",
  "$notes": [
    "Button size (owner ruling, 2026-10-08): size.cta is the action-bar height for every button kind, not only the primary: in a window's action bar (the footer row holding the primary CTA, in a window, a sheet or a modal) every button is the CTA's size (GlassButtonSize.bar). size.controlLarge is the inline size: glass and destructive buttons inside cards, rows, fields, popovers and toolbars (GlassButtonSize.inline, the default).",
    "Window tier: #1146's window-level tokens (--tc-blur-window, --tc-blur-popover, --tc-blur-scrim, --tc-rim-window, --tc-rim-width, --tc-shadow-window and the three --tc-scene-glow colours) have no entry here. On macOS the native material does that work: panes are Liquid Glass on macOS 26 and the HUD vibrancy material before it, the window has no rim of ours, and the scene is the desktop. A shell with no native material would need them back.",
    "Opacity: disabled (0.45) is the one disabled dimming for every control, #1146's --tc-cta-disabled-opacity; the submit pill and the checkbox, which #1146 dims to .55 and .7, use it too. The submit pill keeps its statusOff ink when disabled. rowOff (0.6) is a list row that is off, #1146's .tc-list-row[data-off]. At 0.6 a faded textTertiary sub-line is about 3.9:1 on the pane, so an off row sets its sub-line in textSecondary, which faded clears 4.5:1 (TextContrastTests)."
  ],
  "version": 1,
